WEBVTT

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.240
Commander Asuno!

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.320
Have you discovered anything, Dique?

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.620
I've analyzed what I can, but I don't have the equipment here to do more.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.410
All I can tell you is that thing's unbelievable.{But I know one thing - it's unbelievable. }

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:22.830
Really?

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.540
Its response speed totally outclasses our current mobile suits.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.510
It's packed with engineering marvels that we could only dream about.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.430
It's the perfect fighting machine.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.720
By the way, you know what that is, right?

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:38.430
Yeah.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.980
This device seems to forcibly draw out X-Rounder ability.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.980
It stimulates the X-Region in the brain with a magnetic pulse,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.650
thus allowing the pilot to exhibit powers resembling X-Rounder abilities, if only partially.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.110
But, if they do that...

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.160
Yes.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:03.120
Forcibly activating the X-Region will most likely have a detrimental effect on normal brain function.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.920
If a pilot keeps using it, he'll eventually suffer serious brain {Gun}damage.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.970
But we won't know for sure until we get the autopsy report on the dead pilot.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:19.970
A perfect mobile suit and a helmet that draws out X-Rounder powers...

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.220
No wonder they're so strong.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.680
Dique, I want you to analyze that.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.770
I have to inform Big Ring about this.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.730
Got it.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.280
A helmet that draws out X-Rounder powers...

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.910
If I just had that helmet, I could...

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.370
Vagan.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:56.800
A new nation created by those abandoned in the Mars Sphere after the failed settlement plan.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.430
Forced to live in this harsh environment,

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:11.900
the Vagan began a grand plan to take back the paradise known as Earth.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:23.160
ai ja nai sawarenai

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:23.160
It's not love; I can't touch you

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:28.870
tada hakanai negai deshita

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:28.870
I just had harbored some fleeting wishes

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:34.590
kimi dake sore dake

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:34.590
Wishes about you, no more

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:40.090
mitsumeteita hikari deshita

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:40.090
I stared at the light that was you

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.060
ima unmei wo hamidashite

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.060
Now we break free of fate

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:51.520
sutorobo no toki ga kimi wo sarau mae ni sa

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:51.520
before a time of uncertainty blows you far away

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.480
motto hayaku kakenuketeyuku

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.480
We will go faster than ever before

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:01.110
ano hoshi ni naritai

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:01.110
I want to be your star

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:07.250
maboroshi demo ii

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:07.250
I don't mind if I can never become it

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:14.090
oikakete chiri ni naru made

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:14.090
It's my goal until I turn to dust

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.380
ima ginga wo matataite

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.380
Now I shine onto the galaxy

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:25.850
monokuro no yume ga boku wo sasou mae ni sa

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:25.850
before despair sneaks into my dreams and hopes

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.810
konya mayowazu ni mune wo saku

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.810
Tonight we act without hesitation, without regard for others

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:36.480
ano hoshi ni naritai

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:36.480
I want to be your star

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.070
Did you finish with the check?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:48.790
{TS}Episode 25 
The Terrifying Mu-szell

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.240
Yeah, it’s amazing.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.370
I'm amazed it didn't explode.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.710
Aren't you going to go see it?

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.040
The enemy's mobile suit head, that is.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.380
Oh, no I'm all set.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.420
I'm going to give it a good inspection once everyone else is finished with it.{She's okay with used goods, Obright ;] }

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.800
I see.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:03.550
Yes.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.350
We're in a war, aren't we.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.770
Well, I thought I knew that.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:19.530
But when I saw the dead pilot, it hit me again.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.030
We pilots never know when we're going to die.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.160
Maybe tomorrow...

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:28.330
No, even now, a deploy order could be issued,

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.500
and I may never come back.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.750
That's why...

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.750
so that I can die at any time without regret,

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:40.170
I always want to make sure I have no unfinished business.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.510
Lieutenant?

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.550
So, there's something I want to tell you!

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.180
Y-Yes?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:48.970
What is it?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.770
You may think it’s strange for me to say this to you so suddenly,

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.270
and we've never even gone out together,

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.940
but we've... eaten together in the mess hall, but...

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.480
that's just a small thing—

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.610
No, I mean, there's something more important than all that!

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.150
Um, I don't really understand what you're saying...

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.450
Sergeant Major Ruth!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.910
Y-Yes!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.370
Would you...

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.540
Would you...

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.540
please marry me?!{what a dumbass}

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.130
Sergeant Major...{to be fair, i'd want to marry her too}

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.800
Um, well..

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.140
I'm sorry!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.720
Now he's done it.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.270
There's no way that's happening.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.690
Commander Asuno!{HEY! He decided to call his dad Commander}

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.150
What?

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.320
Please let me use that helmet.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:54.080
If that helmet really draws out powers equal to an X-Rounder's, let me use it!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.960
Then, I'll be able to defeat even more enemies than before!

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:57.870
No.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.290
That helmet is dangerous.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.210
I cannot permit its use.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:04.130
But!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.130
This discussion is over.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:13.390
<i>If I just had that helmet, I would be stronger!</i>

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.650
<i>I could defeat Zeheart!</i>

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.480
My humblest apologies, Lord Ezelcant.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:30.910
As commander, I take full responsibility for the failure of the operation to capture Big Ring.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.410
I am ready to accept whatever punishment you deem fit.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.460
My plan encompasses all possible outcomes.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:43.130
You have achieved the minimum goal of the "Capture Big Ring" operation.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:48.550
During the operation, I was able to gauge the strength of the EFF.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:54.100
Their deployment strategies, their adaptability, their X-Rounder power...

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.100
That is the information we've obtained by sacrificing a few soldiers.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:02.230
Based on the data you obtained, I have finally finished it.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:05.520
A perfect invasion strategy.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.280
A perfect... invasion strategy?

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.780
That's right.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.570
This strategy will not fail.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.490
Let us begin, Zeheart.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.120
Our hope; the creation of our New World.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.160
Yes, sir.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.210
What?! You're kidding, right?

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.000
Why are our sorties cancelled now?

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.760
You even agreed to let us avenge Gren and Zel, Captain!

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.550
The next operation has been decided.{o hai kaiba, wiat where's yugi?}

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.970
We will also be deployed.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:37.930
If you call yourself a solder, you will not disobey your commander's orders.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.770
Are you serious?

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:46.230
Between our pride and that kid's orders, it's obvious which is more important. {- our pride, or that kid's orders!}

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.940
I agree with Lessie.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:54.120
Even among X-Rounders we are the elite of the elite.{missing comma?}

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.950
The Magicians Eight.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:59.620
For us to willingly withdraw without avenging our comrade...

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.080
is not beautiful at all.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.960
Do you feel the same, Mink?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.920
Yes.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:10.340
So much so that I want to take off and lead the attack myself.{Enough that I want to just take off and do it own my own.}

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.430
How about you, Captain?

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.430
Are you really going to {say you'll}try and stop us?

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.100
Oh?

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:24.310
Well, aren't you all having an interesting conversation in here.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.070
You...

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.190
Did you just hear...

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:35.280
We can't have you disregarding the commander's orders and going out on your own.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.990
Don't make that face at me.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.830
I'm not going to tattle on you.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.710
I'm coming with you.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.420
You have no problem with that, right?

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.260
Mobile suit launch?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.970
This is the Downess command center. Respond.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:55.890
Who's in there?!

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.550
We haven't given any order to launch!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.260
Desil Galette,

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.430
Mink Leiden,

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.890
Lessie Adonel,

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.230
and Leo Luis. Four units.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.270
Call them back immediately!

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:07.860
No, there's no point. Leave them be.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:08.810
But...

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:13.820
I don't want the Earth Federation to pick up on our movements by intercepting any careless transmissions.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:15.860
Understood.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.040
I'm coming now.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:25.960
Wait for me,

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.210
Flit!

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:42.350
Unmanned patrol craft R33, S31

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.810
detecting fluctuation in the infrared spectrum.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.730
Unmanned patrol craft T30 confirms.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.730
Consistent with waste heat from a Vagan ship.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:52.820
All right. Commander Asuno's prediction was correct.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.530
The enemy's target is probably...

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.200
Nortram... is it?

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.530
Yes.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:03.080
It's an indispensable colony in intermediate circular orbit above the defenses of the Earth Sphere.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:07.410
It's a weapons production facility as well as a general command center.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:14.300
If Nortram falls, the Earth Federation's strategies will fall apart, and the enemy will easily be able to invade Earth.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.840
That why we had such a hurried departure from Solon City...

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.680
Algreus is in command of the fleet and heading towards it.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.520
Even this ship will be part of our plan.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.020
Understood.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.690
We will put forth all our effort.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.060
Report.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.230
Signal on enemy detections systems.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.280
Unknown units at Bow 442. Four of them.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:35.990
These are...

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.530
Vagan mobile suits.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.200
I came, Flit!{LOL}

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.330
Come on, let’s play!

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.870
This is...

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.710
Desil and the X-Rounder squadron!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:51.630
Why now...?{At a time like this...}{www}{you sicken me, cardslash}

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:54.550
All hands, battle stations!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.130
<i><i>All hands, battle stations!</i></i>

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.300
<i><i>Mobile suits, prepare to launch!</i></i>

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.220
<i><i>I repeat, all hands, battle stations!</i></i>

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.140
<i><i>Mobile suits, prepare to launch!</i></i>

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.140
The enemy's coming!

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:06.270
I hear it's the X-Rounders!

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.980
Are you serious?

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:09.980
They said the black one's coming.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.650
<i>It's not Zeheart?</i>

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.650
<i>But, they said X-Rounders...</i>

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.740
<i>I won't be able to do it as I am now!</i>

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.250
<i>Not like this!</i>

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.170
Asemu?

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.460
Is Asemu late again?

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.260
Tell him to get down here right now.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.670
Understood.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.050
Listen up, the enemy are X-Rounders.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.390
Stay close.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:45.760
Roger!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.890
Woolf Enneacle, G-Bouncer, going out!

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:04.490
There it is.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:12.290
As long as I have this...

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.460
What are you doing here?

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.300
Here they come.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.180
Move it, grunts!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:32.310
Damn.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.570
We're your opponents!

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.320
I know you're in there!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.110
If you won’t come out, I'll blow you apart with the rest of the ship!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.410
Flit!

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.700
Weapons, rapid fire mode.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.700
I will manually input the details.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.410
Set the firing interval to one shot per second.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:14.440
What?

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.560
I can predict your movements, Desil!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.900
What's going on with the AGE-2?

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.610
Why hasn't it launched yet?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:25.950
Um...

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.200
Why are you here?

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:29.870
What are you going to do with that?

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:35.120
I... want to use this while I fight!

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.040
Please, let me do it!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.750
That's ridiculous!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.960
It's to defeat the Vagan X-Rounders!

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:44.380
I need to have power that can compete with them!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.300
No, no you can't!

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:53.060
This damages your brain!

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:57.600
Put that stuff out of your head and get to the mobile suit deck!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:58.690
Got it?!{How convenient, a crow bar}

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.170
These guys...

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.590
They're all pushovers except for the white one.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.100
Especially those two blue ones.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:38.560
Ensign Max!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.910
Arisa! Max!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.080
Die, Earthers!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.350
At least may the flowers of your lives

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:15.680
scatter beautifully!

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:25.860
What?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:32.870
Gundam...

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.240
Ensign Max, Arisa, get back!

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:36.870
Yeah!

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.040
Okay!

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.750
I'm sorry for being late, Commander!

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.590
You... that...

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:52.130
Asemu!

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:53.720
I'll call him back right away.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:57.010
No, in this situation, we must let him fight.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:58.810
Understood.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.650
How dare you...

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.730
How dare you damage my beautiful machine!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.190
You bastard!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:19.620
Asemu!

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.790
You don't have time to look away!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.340
Hey hey, what's wrong?!

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:43.690
I can see it!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.110
This is an X-Rounder's power?

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.910
Don't underestimate me, Earther!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.370
I'll chop you into little bits!

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.390
Impossible... I...

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.980
This isn't beautiful at all!

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:27.900
Leo!

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.320
How dare you kill Leo!

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.300
I've got you!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:03.640
You're not getting away!

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.730
Mink!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.230
As if I'd let you!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:12.520
You're too full of yourself, Earther!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.790
I'm... being pushed back...{That's what she said}

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:39.630
I'm one of the Magicians 8!

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.090
Don't underestimate me!

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:54.360
I don't care about some ability that predicts how I'm going to move!{DRAMATIC SPEECH}

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:04.830
This is <i>my</i>  ability.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.700
Lessie!

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.500
How dare you... how dare you!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.500
I won’t let you get away!

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.340
Wh-What's this?!

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:23.010
Hey, are you okay, Asemu?!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:29.600
What will you do? Keep fighting this battle alone?

